From 66648fbac8fc56dc6d6b6e70a1182b84589b8915 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:28:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] The Prose Portal is its own package

It was part of haiku.hpkg -- the driver, the daemon and a service in the
system's launch script -- which made updating it mean replacing the whole
system. packagefs resolves one file per path, so a second package cannot
supply what the base one already does: the only way to make the portal
replaceable on its own is for the base package not to carry it.

So prose_portal.hpkg carries all three, and the image gets it beside
haiku.hpkg. A newer Prose can then drop in a newer one; nothing else in
the system has to move.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0061-the-prose-portal-is-its-own-package.patch f711c727155be2aed3d9f2a9aafe6e85347edc2d1b239d1a438954f5ba2f0003
---
